<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>The Battle of Palmdale, 1956</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P&gt;This scenario is a recreation of the 1956 "Battle" of Palmdale. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;On this day in 1956, an F6F-5K Target Drone was launched from Naval Air Station Point Mugu for a weapon test. Shortly after take off, the drone stopped responding to radio control signals, and therefore became a runaway airplane. &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Point Mugu had no avaliable assets to shoot it down, so the nearby Oxnard Air Force Base was called to send up fighters to stop the runaway drone. A pair of F-89D Scorpions were dispatched.......&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;U&gt;Historical Outcome: &lt;/U&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;The F-89Ds, armed only with 'Mighty Mouse' Rockets, were unable to shoot down the drone despite expending all ordinance. The drone eventually ran out of fuel and crashed near Palmdale, giving the incident it's name, after flying all over Los Angeles and Ventura Counties.&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Can you succeed where the real pilots failed? &lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;Scenario by Jacob 'Half Life Expert' Douglas&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
